    "@type": "urpx:RatePlan",
    "@id": "smud:tod-low-use",
    "urpx:name": "Rate Schedule R-TOD Time-of-Day (Low Use) Rate (RTL1)",
    "urpx:ratePlanUniqueIdentifier": "RTL1",
    "urpx:initialEffectiveDate": "2026-01-01",
    "urpx:timezoneIdentifier": "America/Los_Angeles",
    "urpx:hasRatePlanVersion": {
      "@type": "urpx:RatePlanVersion",
      "@id": "smud:tod-low-use-2026-01-01",
      "urpx:description": "SMUD Time-of-Day (Low Use) Rate (rate category RTL1) — an optional residential TOU rate available as of January 1, 2026 for customers with constrained electrical service and low usage. Eligibility (per Schedule R-TOD Sec I.B): customer must have panel size ≤ 125 amps AND must be a low-usage customer (typical threshold ≤ 270 kWh/month specific usage cap not enumerated in the source PDF — eligibility is by SMUD review). Estimated ~12K SMUD residential customers (~2% of the residential base). Same TOU window structure as the default Time-of-Day (5-8 p.m.) Rate (RT02) — Peak 5-8 p.m. weekdays non-holiday, Mid-Peak surrounding-summer hours, Off-Peak overnight + weekends + holidays + non-summer. Different rate VALUES from RT02: lower System Infrastructure Fixed Charge ($17/month vs RT02's $27/month) but HIGHER per-kWh prices across all TOU periods (Peak Summer $0.4154 vs RT02's $0.3765, etc.). The fixed-vs-variable trade-off is designed to be advantageous for genuinely low-usage customers — break-even point is around 270 kWh/month, above which RT02 (or the Schedule R Fixed Rate) would be cheaper. Same source PDF (1-R-TOD.ashx) and same Board Resolution (25-06-15 adopted June 19 2025) as the RT02 and RTC1 sub-rates that share the R-TOD schedule umbrella. PCIA / Cost Responsibility Surcharges N/A — SMUD is a vertically-integrated municipal utility, not a CPUC IOU. Plug-In Electric Vehicle Credit (-$0.0150/kWh midnight to 6 a.m. for residential EV-owners) applies via the smud:pev-credit modifier (Sec II.D of source PDF — applies to RT02, RTL1, and RTC1).",
      "urpx:effectiveDateTime": "2026-01-01T00:00:00",
      "urpx:changeReason": {
        "@id": "urpx:rateCase"
      },
      "urpx:priceCurrency": "USD",
