          "@id": "smud:er-residential-tod-low-use",
          "urpx:name": "Eligibility for Schedule R-TOD Time-of-Day (5-8 p.m.) Rate",
          "urpx:description": "Customer is a residential customer who has elected SMUD's optional Time-of-Day (Low Use) Rate (RTL1). Per Schedule R-TOD Sec I.B: customer must have panel size ≤ 125 amps to be eligible. Additionally, the rate is intended for low-usage customers (epic note ~270 kWh/month threshold; specific usage cap not enumerated in source PDF — SMUD-reviewed eligibility). Optional rate; customer may elect RT02 (default Time-of-Day) or Schedule R (Fixed Rate) as alternatives. Eligibility encoded as a residential-customer + 'Optional Rate Election' = 'TOD Low Use' predicate; the panel-size and usage-cap conditions are documented in description prose but not modeled as structural ConditionExpression operands.",
          "urpx:hasConditionExpression": {
            "@type": "urpx:ConditionExpression",
            "@id": "smud:cx-residential-tod-low-use",
